          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "でむかえる — demukaeru — \"to go out to meet (someone arriving)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "くうこうで そふを でむかえました。 — kūkō de sofu o demukaemashita — \"We met my grandfather at the airport.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite でむかえます, demukaemasu; an ichidan verb. Past (polite): ははが くうこうで そふを でむかえました。, haha ga kūkō de sofu o demukaemashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "でむかえる (demukaeru) is a native Japanese word (wago), inherited rather than borrowed from Chinese, built from de, \"going out\" (from deru) and mukaeru, \"to welcome\"; its kanji were attached later as kun'yomi (JMdict)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
